{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Your fathers</b> — Behold, the reproved and the reprovers have died, and you shall know that my words and my prophecy overtook your fathers — the meaning is that they came upon them and they confessed." "And the meaning of \"as he purposed\" — that He knows their deeds before they do them. And Yefet said: the meaning is, know that prophecy has ceased, and this is the meaning of \"Shall they live forever?\" — only the words of the Torah and statutes, did not your fathers overtake them? For in the Torah it is written, \"If you return to HaShem, He will restore your fortunes\" (Deuteronomy 30:2-3); therefore they turned and confessed."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {1 "The phrase כאשר זמם does not appear in the verse text of Zechariah 1:5 as canonically known; its source within Ibn Ezra's discussion is uncertain, possibly a paraphrase of language from v. 6."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:45:37.066787213Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}